# A captured fixture must be the SAME BYTES on every machine.
#
# Git rewrites line endings on checkout by default, and on Windows that turns
# every "\n" in this file into "\r\n". The descriptors themselves are hex, so
# the damage lands on the line ends and hex decoding fails -- which is how it
# was found. A witness that a checkout may edit is not a witness.
testdata/** -text
